  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The puff stitch square places a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "puff"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "puff stitch"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " at the centre of each side on every round above round 1, contrasting a soft, pillow-like bulge against the flat "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "treble"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "treble"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " clusters and chain-2 corners. Puffs are softer and more rounded than bobbles; they bulge gently forward rather than projecting at a sharp angle, giving the square a cushion-like character. The puff is worked as five half-completed trebles closed together: yarn over, insert hook, pull through, yarn over, pull through two loops (leaving two loops on hook) repeated five times, then yarn over and pull through all loops at once."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "infoPanel",
        "attrs": {
          "variant": "materials"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Yarn: DK weight cotton, approximately 32 m per motif. Hook: 4 mm. Notions: tapestry needle, scissors."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "4 rounds in DK cotton with a 4 mm hook = 11 x 11 cm. Puffs pull in the fabric at their position slightly; if your puffs are very tight the square may measure smaller than 11 cm. Ease the tension on the closing loop of each puff stitch if needed."
          }
        ]
      },
