      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Note: ch 3 counts as first tr throughout. Puff stitch: (yarn over, insert hook into st, yarn over, pull through) x5, yarn over and pull through all 11 loops on hook. Ch 1 to close."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 1"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-ring"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic ring"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Ch 3 (counts as first tr). 2 tr into ring. Ch 2. *(3 tr, ch 2)*; repeat 3 more times. Pull tail to close. Join with "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "slip-stitch"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "sl st"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " to top of ch 3. (12 tr, 4 ch-2 corners.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 2"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st to corner sp. Ch 3. *(3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) into corner sp, ch 1, work 1 "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "puff"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "puff stitch"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " into the ch-1 sp between the two side clusters (or into the side space), ch 1*; repeat from * to * 3 more times. Join with sl st. (24 tr, 4 puffs, 4 ch-2 corners.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 3"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st to corner sp. Ch 3. *(3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) into corner sp. Along each side: ch 1, 3 tr into next ch-1 sp, ch 1, 1 puff into top of puff from round 2, ch 1, 3 tr into next ch-1 sp, ch 1*; repeat from * to * 3 more times. Join with sl st. (36 tr, 4 puffs, 4 ch-2 corners.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 4"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st to corner sp. Ch 3. *(3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) into corner sp. Along each side: ch 1, 3 tr, ch 1, 3 tr, ch 1, 1 puff, ch 1, 3 tr, ch 1, 3 tr, ch 1*; repeat from * to * 3 more times. Join with sl st. Fasten off. (48 tr, 4 puffs, 4 ch-2 corners.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "craftChart",
        "attrs": {
          "slug": "crochet-motif-puff-square"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in tails. Light wet-blocking sets the corners square; avoid flattening the puffs under heavy tension as you pin. The puff dimension is part of the intended texture."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Joining"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Join with a sl st seam through the top of the outer treble clusters on each side, or use a join-as-you-go at the ch-1 spaces of the final round."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Hand wash in cool water. The puff stitches can flatten with machine washing; hand washing and reshaping while damp preserves their rounded profile."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The sunburst square motif also uses a raised element at the centre (double treble spikes), but radiating outward rather than sitting at the sides. The lace square motif replaces the side clusters with chain arches for a completely different texture in the same square format."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
